meta {
  name: Checkout Basket (Declined)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/basket/checkout
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "billingAddress": {
      "firstName": "John",
      "lastName": "Doe",
      "emailAddress": "john.doe@example.com",
      "addressLine": "1 Billing Street",
      "country": "USA",
      "state": "Billing State",
      "zipCode": "10001"
    },
    "payment": {
      "paymentMethodId": "pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined"
    }
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 402
  res.body.code: eq "basket.checkout.payment-declined"
}

docs {
  Checks out with a payment method the provider declines. Expect `402` with code `basket.checkout.payment-declined`; the basket is kept, so the customer can retry with another payment method.

  Other test ids the `payment-provider` service declines, with Stripe's codes:

  - `pm_card_visa_chargeDeclined`: `card_declined` / `generic_decline`
  - `pm_card_visa_chargeDeclinedInsufficientFunds`: `card_declined` / `insufficient_funds`
  - `pm_card_chargeDeclinedExpiredCard`: `expired_card`
  - `pm_card_chargeDeclinedIncorrectCvc`: `incorrect_cvc`
  - `pm_card_authenticationRequired`: `authentication_required` / `authentication_not_handled` (3-D Secure isn't supported by this integration)

  Any other id answers `400` with code `basket.checkout.payment-method-invalid`. With the `payment-provider` service stopped, checkout answers `503` with code `basket.checkout.payment-unavailable`.
}
